[size=5][b]Something not working?[/b][/size]

The fastest way to get a bug fixed is to include the editor's log file:

[list=1]
[*]Open [b]Settings[/b] then [b]Diagnostics[/b] and turn on [b]Diagnostic logging[/b] (it's off by default).
[*]Reproduce the problem: reload the save, make the edit, whatever triggered it.
[*]Back in [b]Settings ▸ Diagnostics[/b], click [b]OPEN LOG FOLDER[/b]. This opens [b]%LOCALAPPDATA%\AbioticEditor\logs[/b] in your file manager; the newest [b]editor-YYYYMMDD.log[/b] is today's.
[*]Attach that file to your report, along with the editor version, whether your save is Steam or Game Pass, and what you were doing when it happened.
[/list]

Crashes and save-write failures are logged even with diagnostics off, so the log folder is worth checking either way.

Please report it in the POSTS tab here, or open an issue on GitHub (there's a bug report template that walks through the steps above). Bug reports and ideas are very welcome.

